{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778596392694,"sessionID":"ses_1e365d096ffekQFXv9aHugPedT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8215a2d74adb4bc8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json"},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"**Description:**\\n\\nWhile attempting to obsolete a term in Protégé following the standard CL protocol, I encountered unexpected behavior: the modification occurred in `merged_import.owl` instead of `cl-edit.owl`.\\n\\nUpon investigation, I found that the term to be obsoleted is also present in `merged_import.owl`, due to an imported `skos:prefLabel` from MBAO. This appears to override the expected editing behavior.\\n\\nI tested removing the term from `merged_import.owl`, and the issue was resolved—only `cl-edit.owl` was modified as expected.\\n\\nSince the `skos:prefLabel` values being imported are typically identical to the term label, this issue could be avoided entirely by excluding `skos:prefLabel` imports from MBAO.\\n\\n**Suggestion:**\\nConsider modifying the import pattern for MBAO to exclude `skos:prefLabel`, as it may be unnecessarily duplicative and is interfering with editing workflows.\",\n3:   \"comments\": [],\n4:   \"title\": \"[Typo/Bug] Obsoleting terms affected by skos:prefLabel import from MBAO\",\n5:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3224\"\n6: }\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"**Description:**\\n\\nWhile attempting to obsolete a term in Protégé following the standard CL protocol, I encountered unexpected behavior: the modification occurred in `merged_import.owl` instead of `cl-edit.owl`.\\n\\nUpon investigation, I found that the term to be obsoleted is also present in `merged_import.owl`, due to an imported `skos:prefLabel` from MBAO. This